<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Tech on InterP Blog</title><link>https://interp.blog/en/categories/tech/</link><description>Recent content in Tech on InterP Blog</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 15 Apr 2022 02:45:00 +0900</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://interp.blog/en/categories/tech/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>VSCodeVim: Moving cursor in a wrapped line</title><link>https://interp.blog/en/vim-wrapping-line-cursor-up-down/</link><pubDate>Fri, 15 Apr 2022 02:45:00 +0900</pubDate><guid>https://interp.blog/en/vim-wrapping-line-cursor-up-down/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I installed &lt;a class="link" href="https://github.com/VSCodeVim/Vim" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;VSCodeVim&lt;/a&gt; into my Visual Studio code to code only with keyboard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://interp.blog/images/2022-04-15-vscodevim.png"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But like above, a long line is wrapped so actually it&amp;rsquo;s a single line but it&amp;rsquo;s shown as multiple lines. In this case, if I pressed &lt;code&gt;k&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;↓&lt;/code&gt; on the first (visible) line, the cursor moves to the next &lt;em&gt;actual&lt;/em&gt; line which I don&amp;rsquo;t want to at all!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="how-to-solve"&gt;How to solve
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Actually it&amp;rsquo;s not a problem but a characteristic of Vim with wrapped line, so I found &lt;a class="link" href="https://vim.fandom.com/wiki/Move_cursor_by_display_lines_when_wrapping" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;a document&lt;/a&gt; as a workaround. Then I could adopt it into Visual Studio code as well.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Firstly, open &lt;code&gt;Settings&lt;/code&gt; page and move to &lt;strong&gt;Vim: Normal Mode Key Bindings&lt;/strong&gt; section. Then you can see &lt;code&gt;Edit in settings.json&lt;/code&gt; button. In the following JSON file, put below blocks will solve the issue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-json" data-lang="json"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;vim.normalModeKeyBindings&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;#34;before&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;lt;Up&amp;gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;#34;after&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;g&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;k&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;#34;before&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;lt;Down&amp;gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;#34;after&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;g&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;j&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>